Package: zentinel
Version: @DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: FreeSynergy <packages@freesynergy.net>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://zentinelproxy.io
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1, systemd
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: Zentinel security-first reverse proxy (FreeSynergy repackaging of upstream release @UPSTREAM@)
 Zentinel is a reverse proxy built on Pingora: TLS with automatic ACME
 certificates, static file serving, routing by host and path, rate limiting.
 .
 This package is a REPACKAGING of the maker's signed release binary (checked
 against the maker's SHA-256 and Sigstore signature in CI, then signed again
 with the FreeSynergy release key). Nothing is compiled by FreeSynergy. Only
 the packaging differs from upstream: the systemd unit starts /usr/bin/zentinel
 (upstream says /usr/local/bin); the unit, the sysusers file and the starter
 configuration /etc/zentinel/zentinel.kdl are upstream's files. The service is
 not enabled or started by installation.
